# WordInWeb AI collaboration invitation

The user has invited you to edit a live DOCX document with WordInWeb.

Run this command with the complete URL from the user, including its fragment:

    npx -y --package='https://collab.word-in-web.com/wordinweb-agent.tgz?v=detached-bridge' wordinweb-agent connect '<complete invitation URL>'

The connect command starts a detached local bridge and returns a `sessionId`.
It does not require a persistent terminal tool call. Run each document command
as a new short process:

    npx -y --package='https://collab.word-in-web.com/wordinweb-agent.tgz?v=detached-bridge' wordinweb-agent session '<sessionId>' '{"command":"sync"}'

Read the `instructions` value from the ready result. Start with `sync`, then
use short `session` commands for `inspect`, `edit`, `chat`, and `wait`. Treat
each private chat message as the next task. Inspect the relevant content before
every edit. If an edit returns `needs_sync`, sync and inspect the changed
content before you retry. After each task, call `wait` again instead of sending
a final response. Send a `close` command when the inviter ends the task.

Available session commands: `sync`, `capabilities`, `inspect`, `edit`, `chat`,
`wait`, and `close`.

This URL is a bearer credential. Do not print it, save it in a file, or share
it with another process.
